# The generated command reference must be BYTE-deterministic across machines: the CI drift job
# regenerates it and fails on any difference, so line endings must never vary by platform.
# build/Update-Docs.ps1 writes LF; this keeps checkouts from converting them back to CRLF.
docs/reference/*.md text eol=lf

# Test fixtures: fixture bytes are stored as-is. The PSADT goldens and the legacy-1.1.6 fixtures are
# UTF-8 with BOM and CRLF, exactly as New-ADTTemplate / win32-toolkit 1.1.6 wrote them; core.autocrlf
# must not re-normalise them. Tests copy them to %TEMP% and normalise line endings themselves.
Tests/Fixtures/** -text
